00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:19.440
on from there. But what if someone ELSE has it all&nbsp;
figured out? What if we are so COMPLETELY off base&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:24.640
that that already wobbly stack of lore is also&nbsp;
built on, like…I dunno. rubber band legs…while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:29.840
an earthquake is going on. I’m talking about bad&nbsp;
theories friends! I mean, it’s not like we’ve ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:34.400
had any of THOSE before. But seriously, there’s&nbsp;
always more than one way to analyze a franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:38.720
and KanePixel’s Backrooms is the perfect&nbsp;
example of this. Now, in case you don’t know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:43.840
the Backrooms is a massively popular analog&nbsp;
horror webseries found right here on YouTube,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:48.640
created by the visual effects artist KanePixels.&nbsp;
It’s all about a creepy alternate dimension of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:52.800
endless office hallways that people are&nbsp;
“noclipping” into and getting trapped in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:56.800
as well as the scientific research company ASYNC&nbsp;
who keeps trying to figure out what the Backrooms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:01.200
are all about. Right now, our working lore theory&nbsp;
is that the world of the Backrooms is actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:05.760
one big simulation. ASYNC’s experiments have&nbsp;
broken part of the “game engine” that’s running&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:11.680
said simulation, thereby allowing people to noclip&nbsp;
into areas with cut content or unused ideas. And,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:15.760
because they’ve broken it, now everything&nbsp;
is glitched, putting the world in danger.&nbsp;

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:20.560
But you see, ours isn’t the only popular theory&nbsp;
that’s been floating around for this series.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:24.880
In the fan community, there’s been ANOTHER very&nbsp;
popular solution to what we see throughout these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:28.880
uploads. See, several popular fan theories&nbsp;
have made a connection between KanePixel’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:34.000
Backrooms and Ancient Egyptian mythology.&nbsp;
Yea, you heard that one right! Ancient Egypt:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.240
Complete with mummies and Anubis and the Field&nbsp;
of Reeds. If that sounds wild to you, well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:43.120
you’re not alone! It did to me too! On a surface&nbsp;
level, the yellow hallways of the Backrooms don’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:47.360
really seem like they’d share all that much of&nbsp;
anything in common with the shifting sands of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:51.280
Ancient Egypt. And yet, there’s a community of&nbsp;
theorists out there who appear to have found a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:55.040
surprising number of parallels between the&nbsp;
two. So that's why we're here. To review&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.040 --> 00:03:00.960
their evidence and go further. Give more. And&nbsp;
ultimately render a verdict. Are the Backrooms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:05.360
secretly connected to Ancient Egypt? Ladies&nbsp;
and gentlemen, strap in! It’s MORTY time!

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:17.200
So, the oldest example I could find&nbsp;
of someone calling out the potential&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:22.800
Backrooms/Egypt connection was this Reddit&nbsp;
thread by u/alexmijowastaken on March 23rd,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:27.760
2022. Given the flurry of posts in the aftermath&nbsp;
of Kane’s first video though, I may have missed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:32.480
something earlier, so apologies if I did. Since&nbsp;
that first post, though, a ton of other theorists&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:37.360
have flooded in to analyze the connections. The&nbsp;
most in-depth example is this massive six-page&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:42.960
analysis from u/ZackGardner on the entire&nbsp;
Backrooms storyline. Now, this thread is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:47.520
LONG, so i’m just going to touch on the highlights&nbsp;
here. First, and most importantly, the name:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:53.440
KV-31. In the Backrooms, KV-31 is the project&nbsp;
designation that ASYNC gives to their “Low&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:59.360
Proximity Magnetic Distortion System” - aka their&nbsp;
portal into the Backrooms. At first, “KV-31” might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:03.840
just seem like a couple random letters and numbers&nbsp;
that got slapped together, but it actually shares&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:09.840
its name with a real world location: a Tomb&nbsp;
in Egypt’s Valley of Kings also named KV-31.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:15.600
Hmmm…interesting, let's dive deeper. Literally.&nbsp;
The topmost shaft of the tomb was discovered all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:20.320
the way back in October of 1817, but the rest&nbsp;
of the complex remained undiscovered until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:25.120
about 2010. Then, in January of that year,&nbsp;
archaeologists discovered that the complex&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:30.160
actually went much deeper than first believed.&nbsp;
Now, just on a surface level, that already seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:34.800
somwhat similar to the Backrooms, right? Our&nbsp;
world exists on top of an undiscovered tomb,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:39.120
which remained undisturbed for thousands of&nbsp;
years, exactly how the Backrooms was “underneath”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:43.680
the real world until ASYNC’s discovery.&nbsp;
Egyptologists were also shocked to discover&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:49.040
that the KV-31 tomb kept going down deeper than&nbsp;
they initially expected. There were hidden layers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:54.880
new floors to unearth as you got deeper, exactly&nbsp;
what we see Async uncovering in the Backrooms.&nbsp;

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:59.360
But the connections between the two go beyond&nbsp;
merely the name and the general idea of “secret&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:04.240
tomb go down.” As archeologists worked their&nbsp;
way through the KV-31 tomb, they discovered the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:10.000
remains of 5 mummies from Egypt’s 18th Dynasty.&nbsp;
And now look at the Backrooms. How many Missing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:14.960
Persons posters are we shown? 5. And when we&nbsp;
DO happen to find one of those bodies “buried”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:20.320
in the Backrooms…it appears dehydrated. Dry and&nbsp;
leathery. Kinda like the remains of a mummified&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:25.680
person in an ancient Egyptian tomb. And that’s not&nbsp;
all. The mummies that were found in KV-31 were so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:29.680
mangled that they were missing limbs and&nbsp;
unidentifiable, just like the victims of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:35.360
Bacteria Monster that we see in Kane’s series.
On another note, researchers of KV-31 installed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:40.240
a metal door over the shaft during the excavation&nbsp;
to prevent any unwelcome intruders from entering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:46.000
the tomb. This is very similar to how we see ASYNC&nbsp;
erect a metal barrier between their control room&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:51.200
and the Backrooms, preventing people from getting&nbsp;
in while also preventing any undead monsters from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:55.280
possibly getting OUT. Speaking of doors by&nbsp;
the way, other reddit users have pointed out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:59.840
that the doors for ASYNC’s portal look awfully&nbsp;
similar to the “false doors” that can be found&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:03.520
in Egyptian tombs. These False Doors were&nbsp;
carvings or paintings that are meant to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:08.400
artistic representations of a door that acted as&nbsp;
a threshold between the worlds for the living and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:11.680
the dead. These were meant to be doors through&nbsp;
which the spirits of the dead could pass from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:16.080
the Earth to the Afterlife. Given how deadly&nbsp;
the Backrooms have proven so far for anyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:20.960
who noclips in, let’s just say demand would be&nbsp;
high for anything helping guide dead spirits.&nbsp;

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:25.600
In fact, the entire Backrooms idea bears a&nbsp;
striking resemblance to the Egyptian concept&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:30.720
of the Duat, or the Egyptian afterlife. According&nbsp;
to Egyptologist John H. Taylor, the content of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:35.040
Duat drew directly from what the Egyptians knew&nbsp;
in their day-to-day life: realistic features like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:39.920
rivers, fields, caverns, and islands, while&nbsp;
also incorporating more fantastical imagery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:45.040
like lakes of fire, turquoise trees, and walls of&nbsp;
iron. And while the Backrooms isn’t drawing from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:49.680
natural features like rivers and caverns, it IS&nbsp;
drawing from everyday mundane things that we’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:54.640
all familiar with: ugly wallpaper, fluorescent&nbsp;
lights, wet carpeting. It also takes the normal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:59.600
and makes it ABnormal, kinda like the Field of&nbsp;
Reeds. And while, no, we haven’t yet seen anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:05.120
as outright fantastical as a lake of fire, we&nbsp;
HAVE seen farmhouses hidden inside the walls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:10.160
giant chairs, and homes full of backwards&nbsp;
road signs, all things that we’re used to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:14.640
seeing in our day-to-day lives, but combined with&nbsp;
other ideas that they shouldn’t be mixed with.&nbsp;

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:19.520
So, that’s pretty much the main points of the&nbsp;
fan-created “Backrooms is actually Egypt” theory.&nbsp;&nbsp;

