00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:08.400
Having laid out all the evidence…what do you&nbsp;
think? Seriously. Let me know down in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:12.240
comments. I’d love to have your thoughts on this&nbsp;
theory, ‘cause here’s the way I see it – I’m not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:16.560
buying it. I love a good off-the-wall theory, and&nbsp;
there have been plenty of times where I’ve been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:20.960
known to stretch REAL hard to get some evidence.&nbsp;
But looking at the whole Egypt connection thing;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:25.760
what’s here is circumstantial at best, and even&nbsp;
worse, doesn’t really add up to all that much.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:30.640
Let’s start here with the biggie, the point to me&nbsp;
that’s the most compelling: The name, KV-31. Yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:35.600
the fact that the ASYNC project name and this tomb&nbsp;
in Egypt line up is a fascinating coincidence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:39.360
but we just don’t have enough evidence to&nbsp;
call it anything beyond that. First of all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:45.360
KV-31 is an entirely unremarkable tomb. It’s not&nbsp;
very big like the seemingly endless Backrooms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:50.000
and it didn’t contribute anything significant&nbsp;
to Egyptian archaeology. But more importantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:55.840
there are HUNDREDS of tombs all around Egypt. It’s&nbsp;
easy to hear a phrase like “Ancient Egyptian Tomb”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.840 --> 00:10:00.320
and think something grand and mysterious like the&nbsp;
pyramids, but in reality, they were just, like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:05.200
fancy basements for burials. When I visited Egypt&nbsp;
ten years ago, I went to a few that were literally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:10.080
in the middle of some guy’s backyard. No joke.&nbsp;
We in the West have this mystique and allure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:14.160
attached to Egyptian tombs, but they’re more&nbsp;
common than the media would have you believe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:19.280
Going back to KV-31. The “KV” stands for Valley&nbsp;
of the Kings, it’s on the West Bank of the Nile&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:26.000
right across from Luxor. And in this one area&nbsp;
alone, there are roughly 63 numbered tombs…KV-01&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:32.960
all the way through KV-63. If Kane had picked&nbsp;
ANY KV number between 1 and 63, this exact same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:37.200
argument could have been made. It seems far more&nbsp;
likely to me that Kane either came up with a cool,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:41.680
sci-fi sounding collection of letters and numbers&nbsp;
that just so happened to coincide with an obscure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:46.080
dig site in Egypt. OR he knew about the numbering&nbsp;
system inside the Valley of the Kings, thought it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:51.120
sounded cool, and used it for Async’s project&nbsp;
name with little thought beyond that. Trust me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:55.600
guys. I get it. I’ve been there. I see a weird&nbsp;
world-building detail like that in a franchise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.600 --> 00:10:59.840
that I love and want to theorize about, and so&nbsp;
I try to reverse engineer it. I Search KV-31&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:03.920
to see what comes up and BOOM! First result:&nbsp;
Egyptian tomb. From there, I would try to look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:07.840
for what else I can add to the theory…what other&nbsp;
connections I could make that could be added to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:12.880
that stack of Jenga blocks. I get why people would&nbsp;
want to go down this rabbit hole cause I would do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:18.400
the exact same thing. So, let’s keep going to get&nbsp;
a sense of how stable the rest of the evidence is.&nbsp;

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:22.480
Let’s look at the so-called connections between&nbsp;
all the doors, shall we? The archaeologists in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:27.920
charge of excavating KV-31 sealed the tomb off&nbsp;
using a metal door, just like ASYNC seals off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:33.360
their entrance to the Backrooms using a metal&nbsp;
door. Sure, that a connection of sorts… but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:37.280
probably doesn’t mean all that much of anything.&nbsp;
It’s far more likely that metal doors were chosen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:42.080
in both circumstances because they’re common&nbsp;
building materials that provide strong protection.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:47.040
That is just what happens when you’re trying&nbsp;
to build a secure door in modern times. And the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:51.600
idea that ASYNC’s portal looks like an Egyptian&nbsp;
False Door? I mean… They’re both multi-tiered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:55.200
rectangular entranceways, but that’s&nbsp;
because…they’re doors. More importantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:58.320
though, the theorists that are drawing the&nbsp;
connection here overlook a major point – the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:03.280
FALSE part of the Egyptian FALSE door. They’re&nbsp;
fake. They were etchings used to simulate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:07.840
REAL doors. Kane’s design for the Backrooms door,&nbsp;
meanwhile, appears to be entirely functional.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:11.360
There’s the main entryway! And it’s surrounded&nbsp;
by cabinets that appear to have the necessary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:15.600
wires and electronics to make the main door&nbsp;
function. This comparison also ignores that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:20.560
False Door carvings were typically taller and&nbsp;
thinner, while Kane’s design is short and squat.&nbsp;

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:24.880
As for the five mummies found within the KV-31&nbsp;
tomb compared to the five missing people that we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:29.440
see called out in Kane’s series? That right there&nbsp;
on the surface, seems like it’d be a really solid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.440 --> 00:12:34.720
piece of evidence, until of course, you do the&nbsp;
research for yourself. There aren’t just 5 missing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:40.880
people that are called out in Kane’s series. There&nbsp;
are actually 6! 6 posters with 6 different people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:45.840
shown in the video Missing Persons, as you can see&nbsp;
right here. It’s shown for a brief moment before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:50.480
the entire scene fades into this line graph. But&nbsp;
what about the bodies that were mangled down there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:55.760
in KV-31? Sadly, if you look into WHY they were&nbsp;
so damaged, things fall apart even further. See,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.760 --> 00:12:59.840
the tomb had been thoroughly robbed throughout its&nbsp;
history, with damage attributed to both ancient&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:03.840
robbers looking for valuables and more modern&nbsp;
robbers stealing the body parts of mummies to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:08.640
sell to tourists; Humans are great. If KV-31&nbsp;
was really meant to connect to the Backrooms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:12.960
that would imply that other people had been&nbsp;
exploring the hallways before ASYNC opened the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:17.600
portal. This graph that we see here in “Missing&nbsp;
Persons” explicitly makes it clear that cases for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:22.400
missing people skyrockets after ASYNC makes&nbsp;
contact with the Backrooms. It's only after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:26.960
they break that seal, that noclipping begins.
And finally, we get to the quote-unquote “Evidence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:31.840
point” about the Backrooms taking modern mundane&nbsp;
places and twisting them into something uncanny,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:36.272
just like the Duat afterlife. And to that I&nbsp;
say…Really? Y…you think that’s evidence? That&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.272 --> 00:13:40.080
is just storytelling technique 101. You&nbsp;
know who else found everyday objects and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:44.320
then twisted them into something uncanny? The&nbsp;
Brave Little Toaster. Honey I Shrunk the Kids.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:48.000
Blues Clues. And something tells me that&nbsp;
I’m not getting away with a Backrooms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:52.720
is Secretly the sequel to Blues Clues theory.
So, what happened here? Why did so many theorists&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:57.920
see ASYNC’s project designation KV-31 and work&nbsp;
so hard to connect it with the KV31 tomb? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:00.560
I don’t blame them for doing so. Like&nbsp;
I’ve said throughout this Theory,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:04.640
it’s a fascinating coincidence, and this amazing&nbsp;
community of Theorists was doing their best to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:08.560
try and put the pieces together. Just to prove&nbsp;
my point here: before deciding whether or not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:11.760
I thought the connections between Egypt&nbsp;
and the Backrooms was even intentional,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:16.080
I did a ton of additional research to see if I&nbsp;
could find anything else that might strengthen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:20.160
this entire theory. Dots that no one else had&nbsp;
connected yet. And if I looked hard enough,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:23.600
yeah, the dots were there, but just like&nbsp;
everything we’ve already talked about,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:27.200
they were just stretched out of the bounds&nbsp;
of reason. For example, one could say that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:32.080
the backrooms wallpaper texture bears a passing&nbsp;
resemblance to a pattern of reeds, potentially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:36.400
another connection to the Duat. But that doesn’t&nbsp;
make a ton of sense because the Field of Reeds is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:36.400 --> 00:14:41.600
the paradise afterlife for Egyptians, rather than&nbsp;
the endless maze-like hell that is the Backrooms.&nbsp;

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:45.600
See, when there’s a mystery where something&nbsp;
connects in an interesting or unusual way, humans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:49.920
like to seek answers. Our brains are hardwired&nbsp;
to find explanations for the unexplained,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:54.080
even if there aren’t any answers. This is&nbsp;
a phenomenon called pareidolia. It means&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:59.120
that people have a tendency to impose meaningful&nbsp;
interpretation onto random data, finding patterns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:03.200
where there aren’t any. Have you ever looked up at&nbsp;
the clouds and seen a face or shape within them?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:07.840
Or seen those pictures of houses that look like&nbsp;
people that occasionally go viral? That’s possible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:12.400
because of pareidolia. Your brain is telling you&nbsp;
that that cloud looks like a dog or that house&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:16.880
is giving you a creepy side eye, not because they&nbsp;
actually are but because it's human nature to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:21.440
patterns within the noise. And that’s what&nbsp;
I think happened with KV-31, and this whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:25.920
nothing burger of ancient Egyptian connections.
A final example here: I thought that we might be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:30.720
able to connect the Bacteria Monsters to Egyptian&nbsp;
tombs, specifically as some sort of manifestation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:30.720 --> 00:15:35.440
of the Curse of the Pharaohs. This was an alleged&nbsp;
curse “cast” upon anyone who broke into an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.440 --> 00:15:40.160
Egyptian tomb. It became popular folklore after&nbsp;
researchers mysteriously died in the aftermath&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:44.240
of opening King Tut's tomb. Though there were&nbsp;
many speculated causes, one of the most popular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:48.960
theories was that there was some sort of ancient&nbsp;
bacteria or pathogen that was dormant in the tomb&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:53.360
that was unleashed by opening it. The curse had&nbsp;
a MASSIVE impact on popular culture at the time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:58.320
It's also worth mentioning that more recently, a&nbsp;
pool of black goo was discovered in a 3000 year&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:02.560
old sarcophagus. I mean, really! That has to&nbsp;
be a clear connection to the Bacteria monster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:06.000
right? But, here’s the thing… There's no&nbsp;
evidence or scientific backing that the “curse”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:10.560
ever existed at all, let alone that it was caused&nbsp;
by Bacteria. Instead, all of the deaths can be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:10.560 --> 00:16:14.880
attributed to more natural causes, like blood&nbsp;
poisoning from a mosquito bite. And that black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:14.880 --> 00:16:18.880
goo in the sarcophagus? Apparently, it was just a&nbsp;
mixture of stuff used as an adhesive to keep the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:24.400
sarcophagi sealed, not anything harmful to humans.
Gotta admit, I really tried to find a genuine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:27.440
connection here, because the idea that there&nbsp;
was an additional layer to the Backrooms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:32.000
that it was hiding some historical epic just&nbsp;
beneath its surface of ugly yellow wallpaper.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:37.200
It’s genuinely awesome; and Egypt is always cool&nbsp;
to talk about. But, everything the community&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:41.840
pointed out can easily be dismissed or debunked,&nbsp;
to the point that I just don’t think that there’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:41.840 --> 00:16:46.160
a whole lot there. The ancient Egyptian&nbsp;
connections were interesting coincidences…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:46.160 --> 00:17:03.840
but that’s all wound up being, Loyal Theorists.&nbsp;
Coincidences. Film coincidences. Aaaaand cut.

